I wasn't able to comment a few days ago. Contrary to your question, I think people are born with different gender ...

The way society sees gender evolves, as times change and attitudes about gender are constantly being challenged and revived. In a welcoming world, people of all gender identities are encouraged to respectfully express their identities. Outside of the discipline of having interesting conversations about how to hold giant structures accountable, many different people hold views on gender. These views can vary widely, so there isn't anything unique to any particular gender category.

